# Security and SEO headers for Cloudflare Pages
#
# IMPORTANT: Preview Deployment Indexation
# =========================================
# Cloudflare Pages creates preview URLs (e.g., branch-name.project.pages.dev)
# that could be indexed by search engines, causing duplicate content issues.
#
# This _headers file cannot add host-based rules. To prevent preview indexation:
#
# Option 1 (Recommended): Cloudflare Dashboard
#   1. Go to Pages project → Settings → Headers
#   2. Add rule: URL pattern "*.pages.dev/*" → X-Robots-Tag: noindex
#
# Option 2: Cloudflare Workers (for complex routing)
#
# Production domain (inevitableeth.com) should NOT have noindex.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://giscus.app https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://giscus.app; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://giscus.app https://www.google-analytics.com; frame-src https://giscus.app; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
